From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A7om <hatter6822@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc/bcm2835_property: Do not answer requests the firmware
 cannot read

The firmware reads a property request through the VideoCore's view of
memory, and a buffer outside it gets no answer. The model instead read
zeros from the unmapped address, wrote its response nowhere and still
raised the mailbox interrupt, so a guest that passed a bad address
(an ARM physical address above the VideoCore's aliases, say) saw a
response and went on as if the request had succeeded.

Check that the buffer is readable through the DMA address space before
taking the request, first its header and then the whole size the header
gives, and log a guest error otherwise. Requests in RAM behave as
before: every BCM283x board maps its RAM into that address space.
---
 hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c b/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c
index 216a746..03ac4cd 100644
--- a/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c
+++ b/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c
@@ -469,11 +469,28 @@ static void bcm2835_property_write(void *opaque, hwaddr offset,
                                    uint64_t value, unsigned size)
 {
     BCM2835PropertyState *s = opaque;
+    hwaddr buf;
 
     switch (offset) {
     case MBOX_AS_DATA:
         /* bcm2835_mbox should check our pending status before pushing */
         assert(!s->pending);
+        /*
+         * The firmware can only reach the buffer through the VideoCore's
+         * view of memory, and never answers when any of it is not there:
+         * the header, then the whole size the header gives.
+         */
+        buf = value & ~0xf;
+        if (!address_space_access_valid(&s->dma_as, buf, 8, false,
+                                        MEMTXATTRS_UNSPECIFIED) ||
+            !address_space_access_valid(&s->dma_as, buf,
+                                        MAX(ldl_le_phys(&s->dma_as, buf), 8),
+                                        false, MEMTXATTRS_UNSPECIFIED)) {
+            qemu_log_mask(LOG_GUEST_ERROR,
+                          "%s: buffer at bus address 0x%08"PRIx64
+                          " is not in memory\n", __func__, buf);
+            return;
+        }
         s->pending = true;
         bcm2835_property_mbox_push(s, value);
         qemu_set_irq(s->mbox_irq, 1);
